<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "streambox">
<!ENTITY author    "leone007">
<!ENTITY title     "Streambox">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.10.14l">
<!ENTITY plugdir   "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY cfgdir    "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&title;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        min="7.0.0"
        icon="streambox.png"
        pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leone007/unraid-mediaserver-tools/main/dist/&name;.plg">

<CHANGES>
###&version;
- Language block: saving failed with csrf token mismatch (Unraid checks the token itself and then removes it from the request); fixed
###2026.10.14k
- Language block: the save button (now Save language) was greyed out, because Unraid disables Apply buttons outside a changed form; it works now
###2026.10.14j
- Language: one setting for all the plugins (Sysbox, Diskbox, Seedbox, Streambox), the Language block at the bottom of each settings page: pages and tiles (Follow Unraid or English) and Discord messages (Follow Unraid, English or Magyar). The Discord cards, the weekly summary and the test message now come in English too; a server that already sends them keeps Hungarian, a new install starts in English
###2026.10.14i
- Needs Unraid 7.0.0 or newer (tested on 7.3.2): the Plugins page no longer installs it on Unraid 6, where it was never tried
###2026.10.14h
- Updates now come from GitHub: the Plugins page checks the raw .plg on github.com/leone007/unraid-mediaserver-tools; the local update server (php -S on 127.0.0.1) and repo.php are removed
###2026.10.14g
- Ezen a heten sav: a bal szel egy vonalban a Jellyfin kartyaival (merve); naptarnezetben a napi kartyak szovege a kartyaval meretezodik, 4 bejegyzes tolti ki
###2026.10.14f
- Ezen a heten sav: a kepek olyan magasak, mint a Megtekintes folytatasa kartyai, 2:3 aranyuak, mint a poszterek, ablakmeretre is kovetik; a naptar- es poszternezetben ugyanakkora; a nap neve es datuma a kartya alatt
###2026.10.14e
- Ezen a heten sav: a cim es a nyil a naptar es a poszter nezet kozott valt, mert a Jellyfin Kozelgo oldala ures
###2026.10.14d
- Ezen a heten sav: a poszterek akkorak, mint a Jellyfin sajat poszterkartyai; a cim es egy nyil a Sorozatok Kozelgo fulere visz; flex gap helyett margok, igy a Jellyfin Media Playerben sem csuszik ossze
###2026.10.14c
- Ezen a héten sav: a poszterek fix magassagot kapnak aspect-ratio helyett, igy a Jellyfin Media Player regi Chromiumaban is latszanak
###2026.10.14b
- Jellyfin heti sav: a sorozat neve es a mar letoltott epizodok cime a Jellyfinbol jon (magyarul); a beallitasok sugoja az uj betolto sort mutatja
###2026.10.14a
- Ezen a héten row in Jellyfin: no more flicker (the row is rebuilt only when the list changes, the countdowns update in place); two views, calendar or posters, the default is a setting and each viewer can switch with two icons next to the title; the row now sits inside Jellyfin's own sections, aligned like the others
###2026.10.14
- This week's episodes on Jellyfin's home page (web client and Jellyfin Desktop): a seven-day row in Hungarian (Ezen a héten), with posters, states and countdowns; Streambox writes week.json and week.js every 2 minutes into a folder mapped read-only into Jellyfin, the JavaScript Injector plugin loads it; new settings: the row on or off and the folder
###2026.10.13b
- This week's episodes: the time column counts down to the expected time (in 1d 12h 46m, overdue 3h 10m, aired 03:00 when it is already here); air time, expected time and the usual delay after airing in the tooltip
###2026.10.13a
- This week's episodes: NEW badge on a new series (its first episode airs this week: Sonarr firstAired in the week, or S01E01 in the week)
###2026.10.13
- This week's episodes (item 55): new band under Now playing, Monday to Sunday by day from the Sonarr calendar, air time and the usual time the torrent shows up (median grab delay from Sonarr history), status In Jellyfin, downloading, late; settings band (Seedbox's Sonarr connection or own, delay per series or indexer, late after N hours); optional Discord message for a late episode, default off. Read-only towards Sonarr and Jellyfin
###2026.10.12
- Settings page in the shared look of the plugin pages: a dark band per part, the label on the left, the controls of one setting on one line, the explanation quiet under them; Apply and Done below
###2026.10.11
- The cron scripts (notifications, weekly summary, smart socket sampler) run only from cron, not when their address is opened in a browser
- Settings: the saved Jellyfin API key and Discord webhooks are no longer sent to the page; an empty field keeps the saved value, a single - removes it
###2026.10.10
- Dashboard look: the row boxes have square corners, so the stripes are straight like in Diskbox
###2026.10.09
- Dashboard look: the Now playing and Recently added rows have a plain background, only the stripe and the badge are colored
###2026.10.08
- Dashboard look: Now playing, Server load and Recently added are dark section bands like in Sysbox and Diskbox, the rows sit in a box under them with a colored stripe on the left (direct play green, direct stream blue, transcode amber, paused grey, movie blue, episode purple); the column header is a muted line instead of a dark band. The look comes from a shared common tile.css
###2026.10.06d
- The server load block (GPU, CPU, power, smart socket) can be hidden with the "Show server load" setting; the new Sysbox tile shows these
###2026.10.06c
- Weekly summary in Discord: every Friday at 18:00 (day and hour are settings) one message lists the movies and series/seasons added in the last 7 days, with year, length, quality, genres and rating, each linked to Jellyfin; own webhook, own switch, "Send weekly summary now" button
###2026.10.06b
- Discord cards: forced subtitles are no longer listed; Hungarian subtitles always come first (they were cut off when a file has many subtitle languages)
###2026.10.06
- New logo: monochrome Streambox icon on the dashboard tile, the Plugins page and the settings menu
- Plugin details: display name Streambox, author leone007, description and full release notes
- Update status: the plugin file is served on 127.0.0.1 only, so the Plugins page can run its update check and report "up-to-date"
- Discord notifier: Hungarian cards for new movies and new seasons (poster, backdrop, overview, quality, audio and subtitles, genres, cast, Jellyfin link); separate webhooks for movies and series; test and preview buttons
###2026.10.05b - 2026.10.05k
- Smart socket (Shelly Gen2+): wall power and monthly kWh next to Server load; 10-minute cron sampler keeps the monthly figure exact
- Live TV: progress bar and time left for the current program (from the guide), program times in the hover text
- Direct stream rows say why (transcode reasons, container change, or the file's container/codecs); hover shows the full details
- Server load: current CPU package power in watts (from intel_gpu_top)
- Jellyfin icon (30px, embedded, inverted on light themes)
- Interlaced sources: 1080i label, 1080i -> 1080p / Deinterlace detail for transcodes (from TranscodeReasons / IsInterlaced)
- Live TV: LIVE label instead of a 0% bar, channel + program title, target resolution for transcodes
- GPU load: read the numbers directly from intel_gpu_top output instead of strict JSON parsing
- Container remux shows resolution and bitrate; device names lose the trailing (IP) part
- Audio-only transcodes are shown as Direct stream; GPU load reports why it is unavailable (gpu_note)
###2026.10.05
- First release: Jellyfin now playing (user, device, direct play / direct stream / transcode), GPU and CPU load, recently added
- Short user names: nicknames on the settings page, automatic shortening otherwise
</CHANGES>

<!-- ========================================================= -->
<!-- ARCHITECTURE SETUP                                         -->
<!-- ========================================================= -->
<FILE Name="/tmp/&name;_setup.sh" Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
#!/bin/bash
PLUG="streambox"
DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/$PLUG"
CFG="/boot/config/plugins/$PLUG"

rm -rf "$DIR"
rm -rf "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/Streambox"
rm -f /tmp/streambox_* 2>/dev/null

mkdir -p "$DIR"
mkdir -p "$CFG"

# Defaults are written only if absent, so upgrades never clobber the settings.
if [ ! -f "$CFG/settings.cfg" ]; then
cat > "$CFG/settings.cfg" <<'EOF'
jf_host="127.0.0.1"
jf_port="8096"
jf_key=""
jf_url=""
streams_max="8"
added_rows="5"
show_load="1"
socket_host=""
socket_id="0"
EOF
fi
chmod 600 "$CFG/settings.cfg"

if [ ! -f "$CFG/nicknames.json" ]; then
  echo '{}' > "$CFG/nicknames.json"
fi

# Jellyfin icon (96x96 PNG), embedded so there is no download or CDN dependency
base64 -d > "$DIR/icon.png" <<'B64'
